<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Architecture Overview

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
High Level System Architecture

Main Modules

The design of the application is based on the MVVM pattern. There are three core components in the MVVM pattern: the model, the view, and the view model. Each serves a distinct purpose. The diagram below shows the relationships between the three components.

The MVVN design pattern is implemented in the application as follows: the 4 th layer is the gRPC wrapper for communication with Record and Verify services.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
PREFIX: SW-H10SG-
TITLE: Design Items

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H10SG-11
TITLE: Data management API
STATEMENT: >>>
The application shall use a streaming communication (API) to store and retrieve data remotely from/to the centralized data storage (Database) to allow seamless and sustainable integration.

The list of API functions is defined in the following protocol document:

Heracles DB API
<<<

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H10SG-12
TITLE: Patients' Data Management
STATEMENT: >>>
The application shall include a centralized and secure data repository for storing and managing all treatment planning data, including patient information, imaging data, treatment plans, and treatment history.

Patient Table will be stored in a secure manner, and data will be encrypted.

The data shall be managed in a relational database, which shall support hierarchical organization based on user flow.

The data shall be stored in the form of JSON-serialized Protocol Buffers based on the communication protocol. 
Each Protocol Buffers structure shall have a dedicated database table with the following fields:

- ID
- Parent ID
- Data (serialized JSON)

<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10SG-55
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H10SG-13
TITLE: High Level System Architecture
STATEMENT: >>>
Approvals Calibration - Heater current configuration.

The application is comprised of two key components: Heracles Device Control console (Indoor application) and Treatment Control console (Outdoor application).

The Heracles Device Control console is integrated within the Heracles device. This application addresses functionalities related to patients, demographic data management, clinical data management, treatment data management, user access, clinical workflows, and system setup and services.

The Treatment Control application must be located in a console outside the treatment room. This is to provide the operator with a safe work environment. It should allow healthcare professionals e.g., radiation therapists (RTT), and physicians to activate the radiation emission for the patient's treatment and to provide tools for physicists to program the system's calibration values.
<<<

