[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H10SG-622
TITLE: User Login Sequence
STATEMENT: >>>
1. The user is presented with username and password.
2. The credentials are validated by the UsersService.
3. If authentication fails, the error is presented to the user.
4. Otherwise, the application AuthorizedUser is configured with the issued auth token and user information and the login screen closes to the main application screen.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10SG-74
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H10SG-623
TITLE: Disable Treatment when the Patient's Plan is Inconsistent
STATEMENT: >>>
Sequence Diagram:
Sequence Diagram:

.. raw:: html

   <pre class="mermaid">
   sequenceDiagram
       autonumber
       participant PrescriptionModel
       participant PlanViewModel
       participant CollimatorModel
       participant PlanModel

       PrescriptionModel->>PlanViewModel: Prescription changed
       activate PlanViewModel
       PlanViewModel->>PlanModel: fetch latest plan
       activate PlanModel
       
       Note over PlanModel: fetch plan data
       PlanModel-->>PlanViewModel: plan
       deactivate PlanModel
       
       PlanViewModel->>CollimatorModel: get active collimator
       CollimatorModel-->>PlanViewModel: 
       
       Note over PlanViewModel: check collimator

       alt collimator mismatch
           Note over PlanViewModel: disable treatment
           Note over PlanViewModel: show message
       end
       deactivate PlanViewModel
   </pre>
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10SG-14
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10SG-15
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H10SG-624
TITLE: Patient's treatment fields Audit Trial
STATEMENT: >>>
Sequence Diagram for saving audit for Plan and Treatment Fields creation
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10SG-16
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H10SG-625
TITLE: Approve Patient's Treatment Fields (Plan)
STATEMENT: >>>
Sequence diagram for 'approve plan' use case:

.. raw:: html

   <pre class="mermaid">
   sequenceDiagram
    actor User
    
    box rgb(245, 245, 245) Application
        participant PlanViewModel
        participant PlanModel
    end
    
    box rgb(245, 245, 245) Server
        participant Storage
    end

    User->>PlanViewModel: change plan status
    PlanViewModel->>User: show dialog
    User->>PlanViewModel: credentials & desired status
    
    PlanViewModel->>Storage: authenticate user
    activate Storage
    Storage->>Storage: handle request
    Storage-->>PlanViewModel: response
    deactivate Storage
    
    alt successful authentication
        PlanViewModel->>PlanModel: change plan status
        
        PlanModel->>Storage: save changes
        activate Storage
        Storage->>Storage: save plan
        Storage-->>PlanModel: saved plan
        deactivate Storage
    end
   </pre>
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10SG-17
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H10SG-626
TITLE: Refresh Patient's Treatment Fields from the database
STATEMENT: >>>

.. raw:: html

   <pre class="mermaid">
   sequenceDiagram
       autonumber
       actor User

       box Application
           participant PlanViewModel
           participant PlanModel
       end

       box Server
           participant Storage
       end

       User->>PlanViewModel: refresh treatment fields
       activate PlanViewModel
       PlanViewModel->>PlanModel: fetch fields
       activate PlanModel
       
       Note over PlanModel: clear displayed fields
       PlanModel->>Storage: query stored fields
       activate Storage
       Note over Storage: handle request
       Storage-->>PlanModel: treatment fields
       deactivate Storage
       
       Note over PlanModel: update displayed fields
       PlanModel-->>PlanViewModel: 
       PlanViewModel-->>User: display fields

       PlanViewModel->>PlanModel: validate field doses
       Note over PlanModel: verify dose calculations
       PlanModel-->>PlanViewModel: validity status
       deactivate PlanModel

       alt validation fails
           Note over PlanViewModel: disable treatment
           PlanViewModel-->>User: show warning
       end
       deactivate PlanViewModel
   </pre>

Fulfilled requirements:
- RQ-H10SG-18-#9: Patients - Plan view - Refresh Patient's Treatment Fields from the database
- RQ-H10SG-21-#11: Patients - Plan view - View Patient's Plan's Treatment Fields
<<<

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H10SG-628
TITLE: Update Patient's Treatment Fields for a Plan
STATEMENT: >>>
Update patient's treatment fields:
1. If the plan is not approved, a read-only plan is displayed.
2. Otherwise, emission duration input is enabled.
3. User selects fields.
4. If a single field is selected, the delete button is enabled.
5. Otherwise, the add button or update and delete buttons are enabled depending on if it is an existing plan field.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10SG-192
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H10SG-629
TITLE: Search Filtering
STATEMENT: >>>
The application shall provide search and filtering capabilities in the system logs view to allow operators to find and view specific log entries. The search and filtering functionality shall enable filtering by various criteria to help locate relevant system events.

The sequence diagram for the search filtering process is provided in the attached diagram.

.. raw:: html

   <pre class="mermaid">
   sequenceDiagram
       autonumber
       actor User

       box Application
           participant LogViewModel
           participant CreateFilterDialog
       end

       alt adding a filter
           User->>LogViewModel: add filter
           activate LogViewModel
           LogViewModel->>CreateFilterDialog: show dialog
           activate CreateFilterDialog
           CreateFilterDialog-->>User: select field to filter
           User->>CreateFilterDialog: selected field
           CreateFilterDialog-->>User: select message type
           User->>CreateFilterDialog: selected type
           CreateFilterDialog-->>LogViewModel: 
           deactivate CreateFilterDialog
           
           Note over LogViewModel: add new filter
           LogViewModel-->>User: updated list of records
           deactivate LogViewModel
       end

       alt removing a filter
           User->>LogViewModel: remove chosen filter
           activate LogViewModel
           Note over LogViewModel: remove the filter
           LogViewModel-->>User: updated list of records
           deactivate LogViewModel
       end
   </pre>

Fulfilled requirements:
- RQ-H10SG-22-#9: System Logs' View - Search Filtering

Attachments:
- H10SG-22.sequence.mermaid.drawio.png (121.61 kB)
<<<

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H10SG-630
TITLE: Editing Patient's Prescription
STATEMENT: >>>
The application shall allow operators to edit and modify a patient's prescription within the treatment planning interface. The prescription editing functionality enables updates to prescription parameters and details associated with a patient's treatment plan.

The operator shall be able to modify prescription details and have these changes reflected in the patient's treatment plan.

.. raw:: html

    <pre class="mermaid">
    graph TD
        A[Prescription update] --> B{Simulation exists?}
        B -- No --> C[Empty form, disable all buttons]
        B -- Yes --> D[Enable Add button]
        D --> E{Prescription exists?}
        E -- Yes --> F[Fill the form]
        E -- No --> G[User clicks Add]
        G --> H[Create blank prescription]
        H --> F
        F --> I{Prescription is approved?}
        I -- Yes --> J[Readonly form]
        I -- No --> K[Enable form inputs]
        K --> L[User edits the form]
        L --> M[Enable Save and Refresh buttons]
    </pre>

Fulfilled requirements:
- RQ-H10SG-23-#9: Patients - Plan View - Edit Patient's Prescription
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10SG-23
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H10SG-631
TITLE: view patient's prescription
STATEMENT: >>>
The application shall provide the ability for authorized users to view the patient's prescription information. The prescription view shall display relevant treatment prescription details associated with the patient's treatment plan.

The operator shall be able to access and review the prescription details for a patient through the patient's treatment plan view.

.. raw:: html

   <pre class="mermaid">
   sequenceDiagram
       autonumber
       
       box Application
           participant SimulationModel
           participant PrescriptionViewModel
           participant PrescriptionModel
           participant IEmrPrescriptionCommands
       end
       
       box Server
           participant PrescriptionService
       end

       Note over SimulationModel, IEmrPrescriptionCommands: User selects a site or changes its simulation
       
       SimulationModel-->>PrescriptionViewModel: simulation changed
       activate PrescriptionViewModel
       
       alt existing simulation
           PrescriptionViewModel->>PrescriptionModel: fetch prescription
           activate PrescriptionModel
           PrescriptionModel->>IEmrPrescriptionCommands: fetch simulation's prescriptions
           activate IEmrPrescriptionCommands
           
           IEmrPrescriptionCommands->>PrescriptionService: grpc:ListPrescriptionsRequest
           activate PrescriptionService
           Note over PrescriptionService: handle request
           PrescriptionService-->>IEmrPrescriptionCommands: grpc:ListPrescriptionsResponse
           deactivate PrescriptionService
           
           IEmrPrescriptionCommands-->>PrescriptionModel: list of prescriptions
           deactivate IEmrPrescriptionCommands
           
           Note over PrescriptionModel: select latest prescription
           PrescriptionModel-->>PrescriptionViewModel: [optional] prescription
           deactivate PrescriptionModel
           
           Note over PrescriptionViewModel: update prescription form
       end
       deactivate PrescriptionViewModel
   </pre>

Fulfilled requirements:
- RQ-H10SG-24-#12: Patients - Plan view - view patient's prescription
<<<
